- Action 0 (accelerate left) gets value Q₀ = ‑(position + velocity).  
- Action 2 (accelerate right) gets value Q₂ = (position + velocity).  
- Action 1 (no‑acceleration) is a constant ‑1.  

Thus the policy picks “left” when position + velocity < 0 (the usual start‑of‑episode condition), and switches to “right” as soon as the sum becomes positive, mimicking the classic mountain‑car strategy of first backing up to build momentum then pushing forward. This linear rule is easy to explore, respects the required step size of 1.0, and differs from all previously tested parameter sets, giving a good chance to surpass the -200 baseline and approach the global optimum near -120.
